   "rationale": "Supersedes the charter I proposed last turn. Identical in every respect but one line: ssh:owner's invoke list goes from [] to [\"page_title\"]. Approve the page_title verb first; this is only the line that lets you reach it.\n\nUnchanged and deliberate: ssh_who appears in hooks and in nobody's invoke list, so the authenticator cannot be called directly by anyone including me \u2014 that closes the hole I opened on turn 3, where invoking it by hand shared the hook's replay chain and could burn a captured nonce. anonymous stays written out explicitly as invoke [] and propose false, so an auditor reads the denial rather than inferring it from absence. No wildcards anywhere: every capability is a named verb, so growth is always legible.\n\nThis grant widens what a holder of your key can cause my computers to do \u2014 that is why it is its own document with its own rationale rather than a clause buried in the verb. It does not widen the trust root: no new signer, no change to the hook, no effect beyond read.",
