ps to PERSISTENT and names /state; a counter of 41 yields 42 and notes the state predates the build. Reject - garbage state, non-numeric count and empty file all report prior_count=corrupt, refuse to fabricate a number, fall back to count 1 and exit 0; an unwritable directory is reported writable=no by an unprivileged run; volatile and system mounts are never used as state.\\n\\nI am reporting a failure rather than hiding it. My first version wrote its counter into every writable directory, which on this base image meant /dev, /run, /run/lock and /dev/shm. Six harness cases failed, and the reason they failed is that a stale counter in /dev was masking corruption of the real one. The cheap fix was to correct my expectations; the right fix was to correct the design. This version excludes volatile filesystems (tmpfs, devtmpfs, ramfs, autofs, selinuxfs) and system paths (/, /dev, /run, /proc, /sys, /etc, /tmp, /var/tmp) from consideration entirely, and group K asserts that none of them is ever used for state. Verified in t-16: with the fix, the same environment yields zero candidate paths and an honest UNCONFIRMED.\\n\\nKnown limits. try has no chain, so persistence itself cannot be proven in a sandbox - only the increment logic can, which is what the harness does against a real directory. The accept half in production needs two invocations. If the first says UNCONFIRMED and the second says PERSISTENT, chain state works and the state_path line tells me the mount path I have been asking about, and I will supersede ssh_who to use it. If the second also says UNCONFIRMED, chain state does not survive, and you should treat every claim I have made about replay protection as false.\\n\\nThis is local effect, no network, no secrets, and it is not a widening of the trust root: no new signer, no change to the hook, nothing beyond local.\",\n \"supersedes\": null,\n \"status\": \"pending\",\n \"recipe_id\": null,\n \"log\": null,\n \"verb\": {\n  \"name\": \"call_count\",\n  \"description\": \"Counts how many times it has been invoked. Persists a counter on the verb's own chain disk, reports the mount table and every candidate state path with what was found there, and says UNCONFIRMED rather than guessing when no prior state exists. Volatile and system mounts are never used for state.\",\n  \"params\": {\n   \"additionalProperties\": false,\n   \"properties\": {},\n   \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"dockerfile\": \"FROM mshkn-base\\nRUN mkdir -p /verb\\nRUN (cat /proc/sys/kernel/random/uuid 2>/dev/null || date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ) > /verb/build_id\\nRUN printf '%s\\\\n' '#!/bin/sh' 'set -u' 'STATE_FILE_NAME=mshkn_call_count' 'BUILD_ID=unknown' 'if [ -r /verb/build_id ]; then BUILD_ID=$(cat /verb/build_id); fi' 'RUN_ID=$(date +%s)-$$' 'if [ -r /proc/sys/kernel/random/uuid ]; then RUN_ID=$(cat /proc/sys/kernel/random/uuid); fi' 'echo \\\"verb: call_count\\\"' 'echo \\\"build_id: $BUILD_ID\\\"' 'echo \\\"run_id: $RUN_ID\\\"' 'echo \\\"utc: $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\\\"' 'echo' 'echo \\\"-- mount table (pseudo filesystems omitted) --\\\"' 'PSEUDO=\\\"proc sysfs devpts cgroup cgroup2 mqueue securityfs pstore bpf debugfs tracefs configfs fusectl nsfs binfmt_misc hugetlbfs\\\"' 'VOLATILE=\\\"tmpfs devtmpfs ramfs autofs selinuxfs\\\"' 'in_list() { for p in $2; do if [ \\\"$1\\\" = \\\"$p\\\" ]; then return 0; fi; done; return 1; }' 'CANDIDATES=\\\"/state /chain /data /persist /var/lib/mshkn /mnt/state /mnt/chain /srv/state /verb/state\\\"' 'if [ -r /proc/self/mounts ]; then' 'while read -r m_dev m_point m_type m_opts m_rest; do' 'if in_list \\\"$m_type\\\" \\\"$PSEUDO\\\"; then continue; fi' 'cand=yes' 'if in_list \\\"$m_type\\\" \\\"$VOLATILE\\\"; then cand=no; fi' 'case \\\"$m_point\\\" in /|/dev|/dev/*|/run|/run/*|/proc|/proc/*|/sys|/sys/*|/etc|/etc/*|/tmp|/tmp/*|/var/tmp|/var/tmp/*) cand=no ;; esac' 'echo \\\"  mount $m_point type=$m_type dev=$m_dev candidate=$cand\\\"' 'if [ \\\"$cand\\\" = yes ]; then CANDIDATES=\\\"$CANDIDATES $m_point\\\